KNOWNBUG
unsatisfied.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ bullet 3: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
See test.desc.  With unsatisfied constrained partial specializations for
B = 1 and 2 ([temp.spec.partial.match]/1: they do not match), impl<int>
must derive from impl<int, 2> and that from the partial specialization
impl<int, 3>.  The front end crashes (SIGSEGV, unbounded recursion between
primary_base and vtable_pointer_component: the class ends up its own
base).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
